  "issue_number": 11315,
  "issue_title": "Concurrent API-token initialization can hang browser tests",
  "issue_body": "### Describe the bug\n\n\nVitest 5.0.0 can accept an empty API token during concurrent first-time startup. In browser mode this causes WebSocket authentication to fail, followed by the default 60-second connection timeout without executing any tests.\n\nOriginally observed in Linux CI with four Vitest processes and three browser workers per process. Separate Vite cache directories do not isolate the user-level `.vitest-secret-token` file. A standalone reproduction now demonstrates both the race and its browser consequence without application code or patched dependencies.\n\n**Expected:** concurrent initialization must not accept an empty token; an invalid token file should be handled explicitly rather than producing an opaque browser timeout.\n\n**Actual:** one process can retain an empty token even after another process finishes writing the file. The browser client sends `\"0\"` instead, so the server rejects its connection.\n\n### Reproduced results\n\n1. Four processes called the public `resolveConfig()` API concurrently against a fresh shared temporary home. On attempt 7, one returned `tokenLength: 0, tokenCreated: false`; the other three returned 36-character tokens.\n2. In a separate deterministic browser experiment, an empty token file caused the single test to time out at 60.00 seconds with no tests executed. Replacing only that file's contents with a UUID made the same test pass in 776 ms.\n\n```text\nError: Failed to connect to the browser session \"7a30d5cb-55ef-45e8-9e4d-c7e0ed85c933\" [chromium] within the timeout.\n```\n\n### Source-level explanation\n\n[`resolveTokenFromPath`](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/v5.0.0/packages/vitest/src/node/config/apiToken.ts#L27-L41) accepts `readFileSync(tokenPath, 'utf-8').trim()` without rejecting empty contents. New files are written directly to the destination with `writeFileSync`.\n\n[INFERENCE] The interleaving consistent with the source and observed empty read is: one initializer opens/creates or truncates the file, another sees it and reads before its contents are written, and the second retains an empty token in memory.\n\nThe [browser client](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/v5.0.0/packages/browser/src/client/client.ts#L22) uses `(window as any).VITEST_API_TOKEN || '0'`. The resulting `\"0\"` does not match the empty server token. The [RPC upgrade handler](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/v5.0.0/packages/browser/src/node/rpc.ts#L61-L64) destroys the socket when token validation fails, before completing the handshake.\n\nOnly released 5.0.0 was runtime-tested. Upstream `main` had the same initializer when inspected, but was not built or runtime-tested. The original failing CI run recorded token validation rejection, not token lengths; the empty-token mechanism was established by the separate standalone experiments above.\n\nAI assistance: OpenAI Codex helped investigate and prepare this report and reproduction.\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n\nhttps://github.com/olivier-thatch/vitest-api-token-race-repro\n\nThe repository contains the complete standalone example and pinned lockfile:\n\n```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/olivier-thatch/vitest-api-token-race-repro.git\ncd vitest-api-token-race-repro\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts\npnpm run race\npnpm exec playwright install chromium\npnpm run reproduce\n```\n\n- **`race`** uses four public `resolveConfig()` calls, synchronized through a Vite `configResolved` hook, with fresh shared temporary homes and distinct cache directories. It does not pre-create tokens, mock filesystem calls, extract private functions, or patch Vitest. This is timing-dependent: it tries up to 80 attempts by default; `pnpm run race 200` increases the limit. Exit 0 means an empty token was observed.\n- **`reproduce`** deliberately creates an empty token in an isolated temporary home, verifies the 60-second browser timeout, then changes only the token contents and verifies a passing control. This is deterministic bad-state reproduction, not the concurrency experiment. The outer command exits 0 only when both results match, and takes approximately one minute.\n- Both scripts leave the normal user token untouched. No token values are logged.\n- Both scripts were verified on macOS arm64. This standalone package has not been run on Linux or Windows.\n\n\n### System Info\n\n```shell\nCollected using the requested `envinfo` options; executable paths and unrelated tools are omitted. The reproduction uses Playwright's installed Chromium, not the system browsers listed by `envinfo`.\n\n\nSystem:\n  OS: macOS 26.7\n  CPU: (12) arm64 Apple M4 Pro\nBinaries:\n  Node: 24.16.0\n  npm: 11.13.0\n  pnpm: 12.3.4\nBrowsers:\n  Chrome: 153.0.8010.52\n  Firefox: 153.0.1\n  Safari: 27.0\nnpmPackages:\n  @vitest/browser-playwright: 5.0.0 => 5.0.0\n  playwright: 1.62.1 => 1.62.1\n  vite: 8.2.2 => 8.2.2\n  vitest: 5.0.0 => 5.0.0\n```\n\n### Used Package Manager\n\npnpm\n\n### Validations\n\n- [x] Follow our [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] Read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n- [x] Read the [docs](https://vitest.dev/guide/).\n- [x] Check that there isn't [already an issue](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues) that reports the same bug to avoid creating a duplicate.\n- [x] Check that this is a concrete bug. For Q&A open a [GitHub Discussion](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/discussions) or join our [Discord Chat Server](https://chat.vitest.dev).\n- [x] The provided reproduction is a [minimal reproducible example](https://stackoverflow.com/help/minimal-reproducible-example) of the bug.",
